# Suppressed dependency findings.
#
# Currently: none. The audit is clean without suppressions, which is the state
# worth defending -- every entry here is a small piece of coverage given up.
#
# Any ID added must be justified in docs/DEPENDENCY_EXCEPTIONS.md with a
# REACHABILITY argument -- "there is no call site", checkable with a grep --
# not a severity opinion. Each carries a review date no more than 90 days out.
# scripts/audit_deps.py refuses to run if an ID here has no written
# justification, so the list and the reasoning cannot drift apart.
#
# Reachable vulnerabilities are never listed here. They are fixed, or accepted
# as risk by a named owner with compensating controls, in the same document.
# A scanner whose suppressions are unargued is decoration.
#
# Consumed by:  make audit-deps  /  the CI supply-chain job
# Format: one vulnerability ID per line; # comments and blank lines ignored.
